                        "form": "surfemme"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "8d72faeb-f4b7-4450-aa25-da492526428a",
                        "entry_id": "2832780e-d11e-3c94-964b-37e43c5c9b10",
                        "tags": [
                            "feminine"
                        ],
                        "form": "superfemme"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b9a969d9-37ab-363d-bd13-7bcad8ce2b41",
                        "entry_id": "2832780e-d11e-3c94-964b-37e43c5c9b10",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Homme considéré comme dépassant au moral la mesure ordinaire de la nature humaine."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "207594b2-8f48-4fc3-b8ca-dffea91dfbbd",
                                "sense_id": "b9a969d9-37ab-363d-bd13-7bcad8ce2b41",
                                "text": "En fait, le surhomme apparait comme l’antitype de l’homme démocratique."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "61447d27-4549-43f0-a355-4094c4d3878b",
                                "sense_id": "b9a969d9-37ab-363d-bd13-7bcad8ce2b41",
                                "text": "Un et un font un lorsque l’addition porte sur l'homme et sur Dieu et qu’on ne confond ni le premier avec un sous-Dieu, ni le second avec un surhomme."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "981c9059-e159-43c2-934f-8b84ec64e4f5",
                                "sense_id": "b9a969d9-37ab-363d-bd13-7bcad8ce2b41",
                                "text": "Le surhomme est seul. Il peut avoir des amis, des complices, mais qui n'arrivent pas à sa cheville. Sherlock Holmes formait un couple avec le Dr. Watson, mais c'est qu'il avait besoin d'un historiographe"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6f9724c5-e7d6-3f89-89c0-d51035ae5d70",
                        "entry_id": "2832780e-d11e-3c94-964b-37e43c5c9b10",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Personne dépassant la force physique ordinaire."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "fdf7d86b-b4fe-4c94-a814-047a40cfda6f",
                                "sense_id": "6f9724c5-e7d6-3f89-89c0-d51035ae5d70",
                                "text": "À dix sur un, ça se croit surhomme"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e55cdd83-3da5-3674-b4ea-cc033b03ee3e",
                        "entry_id": "2832780e-d11e-3c94-964b-37e43c5c9b10",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Dans la pensée de Nietzsche et dans le décadentisme, homme qui accepte la vie terrestre comme unique réalité avec courage, qui redonne du sens à la vie terrestre, ne se faisant pas d’illusion, qui ne fait pas appel à une réflexion rationnelle et qui se dépasse lui-même grâce à la volonté."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "15e201b6-0b53-445d-a327-89112fa733e9",
                                "sense_id": "e55cdd83-3da5-3674-b4ea-cc033b03ee3e",
                                "text": "« Voici, je vous enseigne le Surhomme. Le Surhomme est le sens de la terre. Que votre volonté dise : Que le Surhomme soit le sens de la terre. »"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "6f261e3c-6999-456f-8f00-2c2746ca0386",
                        "source_entry_id": "2832780e-d11e-3c94-964b-37e43c5c9b10",
                        "target_lang_word": "Übermensch",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Übermensch",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e27beaec-a76a-355f-a345-0527d57abae7",
                                        "entry_id": "bda415c9-6c4e-37e7-a2b4-d8fbf2279870",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "idealer Mensch, der geistig über gewöhnliche Menschen hinausgewachsen und zum Herrschen bestimmt ist"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "53789606-efee-4b29-adea-60e7f90d38e3",
                                                "sense_id": "e27beaec-a76a-355f-a345-0527d57abae7",
                                                "text": "Der Philosoph Friedrich Nietzsche schrieb, dass es noch nie einen Übermenschen gab, Johann Wolfgang von Goethe oder Napoleon Bonaparte kamen ihm allerdings schon nahe an das Bild des Übermenschen heran."
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c99533b7-0110-4e97-8b75-70cda3d3f667",
                        "source_entry_id": "2832780e-d11e-3c94-964b-37e43c5c9b10",
                        "target_lang_word": "superman",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "superman",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "14e56556-a3ea-3d3f-874d-980dd0ebbdbc",
                                        "entry_id": "f02ddf65-ed68-3908-8258-d71d51bcb82f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An imagined superior type of human being representing a new stage of human development; an übermensch, an overman."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4e72997b-40c8-4809-8ce1-79fa794bab28",
                                                "sense_id": "14e56556-a3ea-3d3f-874d-980dd0ebbdbc",
                                                "text": "Nietzsche wrote of the coming of the superman."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4ef0a5b0-83ef-46c3-9235-ad84163669d7",
                                                "sense_id": "14e56556-a3ea-3d3f-874d-980dd0ebbdbc",
                                                "text": "Man does desire an ideal Superman with such energy as he can spare from his nutrition, and has in every age magnified the best living substitute for it he can find. His least incompetent general is set up as an Alexander; his King is the first gentleman in the world; his Pope is a saint. He is never without an array of human idols who are all nothing but sham Supermen."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7ef972d7-ffd7-4084-909a-29b2607a1be6",
                                                "sense_id": "14e56556-a3ea-3d3f-874d-980dd0ebbdbc",
                                                "text": "And Zarathustra spake thus unto the people: / I teach you the Superman. Man is something that is to be surpassed. What have ye done to surpass man? / … What is the ape to man? A laughing-stock, a thing of shame. And just the same shall man be to the Superman: a laughing-stock, a thing of shame."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1d057a8c-3aca-48aa-bfc8-b8dd240822c9",
                                                "sense_id": "14e56556-a3ea-3d3f-874d-980dd0ebbdbc",
                                                "text": "\"Well, what is it that he does that I don't do? Just say the word, - teetotal, vegetarian, aeronaut, theosophist, superman.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fba02687-622f-3829-b1cd-4696ddaaeb0f",
                                        "entry_id": "f02ddf65-ed68-3908-8258-d71d51bcb82f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A man of extraordinary or seemingly superhuman powers."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d261de7f-c14b-4f8a-9834-2e0a8827ca48",
                                                "sense_id": "fba02687-622f-3829-b1cd-4696ddaaeb0f",
                                                "text": "[page 113] The idea of superman is as old as the world. Through all the centuries, through hundreds of centuries of its history, humanity has lived with the idea of superman. Sayings and legends of all ancient peoples are full of images of a superman. Heroes of myths, Titans, demi-gods, Prometheus, who brought fire from heaven; prophets, messiahs and saints of all religions; heroes of fairy tales and epic songs, knights who rescue captive princesses, awake sleeping beauties, vanquish dragons, and fight giants and ogres—all these are images of a superman. [...] [page 114] People dreamt of, or remembered times long past when their life was governed by supermen, who struggled against evil, upheld justice and acted as mediators between men and the Deity, governing them according to the will of the Deity, giving them laws, bringing them commandments."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4cc453b1-bbee-4687-a3f7-0292539117ac",
                                                "sense_id": "fba02687-622f-3829-b1cd-4696ddaaeb0f",
                                                "text": "By the latter part of 1848, the throne of Hudson the Railway King who had been called in in 1845 as a superman to save the Eastern Counties Railway, was tottering to its fall, [...]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a9b9badb-f891-4dea-a9ff-5c86c92c5212",
                                                "sense_id": "fba02687-622f-3829-b1cd-4696ddaaeb0f",
                                                "text": "I had a vision of what the ideal man should be. I wanted someone whose income combined with mine could afford us a family, an apartment, a car, and all the travel, luxury, and fun we could possibly tolerate. I wanted a Superman."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "539d9f64-5aea-4191-bfd1-ef75753aca0c",
                                                "sense_id": "fba02687-622f-3829-b1cd-4696ddaaeb0f",
                                                "text": "What type of human weakness might a being of unfathomable power—a superman—inadvertently expose to the keen analytic mind of an avenging dark knight? Would he discover that a superhuman being who cannot be overcome, who is loved and adored by most, and who awes the commoner, desires to be overcome?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0417f122-ef18-4a9d-a54c-cc33f130df8a",
                                                "sense_id": "fba02687-622f-3829-b1cd-4696ddaaeb0f",
                                                "text": "Early in Crime and Punishment, [Rodion] Raskolnikov has become obsessed with the notion that he himself is a \"superman.\" Therefore, he thinks, he is not subject to the laws that govern ordinary people. […] However, his indecision and confusion throughout the novel indicate that he is not a superman. Moreover, in the course of the novel, [Fyodor] Dostoyevsky seeks to prove that there is no such thing as a superman. Dostoyevsky believes that every human life is precious, and no one is entitled to kill."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "de9c525e-cf81-4d67-a01a-2c3dd15fbe21",
                                                "sense_id": "fba02687-622f-3829-b1cd-4696ddaaeb0f",
                                                "text": "Realty experts in the Mexican market say that the cause of the shortages is a slowdown in housing development (Didn’t they tell us we needed illegals to help build more houses to counter the housing shortage in the US? Why don’t they put all these returning construction supermen to work in Mexico?)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b9d5c150-630c-4af4-8d55-299d6c578fb8",
                        "source_entry_id": "2832780e-d11e-3c94-964b-37e43c5c9b10",
